  "system_note": "Billed line: revenue_code 0192, 18 days, DOS range 2026-05-12 → 2026-06-08. Review of the clinical record shows consistent, documented therapy minutes that support a therapy-based per-diem (0192) for 2026-05-12 through 2026-05-27 (daily PT entries of ~90 minutes plus OT where documented; see citations below). The facility did NOT provide explicit per-diem level statements on any dates (get_per_diem_level_notes rows are null), which is acceptable when daily minutes meet the billed level. However, the therapy-session extract and medical record notes returned in this review include documented PT/OT sessions only through 2026-05-27; there are no therapy-session entries returned for 2026-05-28 through 2026-06-08 to substantiate billing 0192 on those later dates. Therefore the record supports revenue code 0192 for 2026-05-12 through 2026-05-27 (16 days) but does not support the billed 0192 level for the remaining billed days within the claimed DOS range. Adjustment: reduce revenue code 0192 units from 18 to 16 (supported DOS 2026-05-12—2026-05-27). Evidence relied on: H&P admission stating patient admitted for “skilled PT, OT and nursing services” (H&P, p.8); Interdisciplinary Plan showing PT/OT frequency and plan (Interdisciplinary Plan of Care, p.10-11); PT evaluation certifying care 05/12/2026–06/11/2026 and treatment frequency (Physical Therapy, p.18-19); daily PT progress notes documenting ~90 minutes of skilled PT (examples: Physical Therapy 05/13, p.24; Physical Therapy 05/22, p.42). The per-diem-level extraction explicitly shows level_determination_statement = null on dates when no explicit facility-level exception was recorded (get_per_diem_level_notes result). Because no therapy-session documentation was returned for 05/28–06/08, those dates cannot be sustained as therapy-level (0192) per-diem days in this audit. ",
  "rationale_letter": "Re: Audit determination for MR_SNF_09 — revenue code 0192 (billed 18 days; 2026-05-12 through 2026-06-08)\n\nDear Provider,\n\nWe have completed our review of the medical record and supporting documentation for the above-referenced SNF claim line. The submitted bill includes revenue code 0192 (therapy-level per-diem) for 18 days from 05/12/2026 through 06/08/2026.\n\nFinding: The medical record supports the billed therapy-level per-diem (rev. code 0192) for dates 05/12/2026 through 05/27/2026 (16 days). The record does NOT contain therapy-session documentation to support revenue code 0192 for dates 05/28/2026 through 06/08/2026; therefore 2 of the 18 billed days are unsupported at the 0192 per-diem level and must be adjusted.\n\nBasis: Documentation shows the patient was admitted for skilled PT/OT/nursing (History & Physical, 05/12/2026) and an interdisciplinary plan specifying PT/OT frequency (Interdisciplinary Plan of Care, 05/12/2026). Daily physical therapy progress notes document skilled PT sessions of approximately 90 minutes on each therapy day between 05/12/2026 and 05/27/2026 (see PT progress notes dated 05/13/2026 and 05/22/2026). The per-diem extraction tool returned null per-diem-level statements (i.e., no explicit facility downcoding statements), which is consistent when daily therapy minutes meet the billed level. However, the therapy-session extract and progress notes produced in the record for this audit contain no PT/OT session entries after 05/27/2026. In the absence of documented therapy minutes on 05/28/2026–06/08/2026, those dates cannot be sustained as therapy-level per-diem days.\n\nCorrection: Reduce revenue code 0192 units from 18 to 16, corresponding to 05/12/2026–05/27/2026 (supported therapy-level days). The remaining billed days within 05/28/2026–06/08/2026 should be billed at the appropriate lower per-diem level (or non-covered) consistent with documentation (e.g., nursing-only per-diem) or be substantiated with additional records if you disagree with this adjustment.\n\nIf you believe additional documentation (therapy progress notes, daily therapy logs, or other bedside therapy records) exists to support 0192 for 05/28/2026–06/08/2026, please submit those records for re-review.\n\nSincerely,\nClinical Audit Team",
