  "system_note": "Reviewed revenue line 2 (billed revenue code 0191) for claim MR_SNF_09 covering 2026-05-12 to 2026-06-08. Available clinical documentation shows multiple days with high therapy minutes (examples: PT 90 minutes + OT 60 minutes on 2026-05-12 and repeating through 2026-05-27), and the facility did not record per-diem-level exception statements for the dates queried (per-diem note entries are null). Policy (fallback reference guide in dataset) defines skilled need as requiring licensed nursing or therapy staff and lists a required prior qualifying hospital stay to establish the skilled need; it also identifies 0191 as a standard per-diem code (0191 = skilled nursing).\n\nHowever, two key evidentiary gaps prevent a full determination for the entire billed date range:\n1) The raw daily therapy rows retrieved only include explicit therapy-session entries through 2026-05-27; there are no retrieved daily therapy-session rows for 2026-05-28 through 2026-06-08, so the audit cannot verify therapy minutes for every billed date in the range. (See cited daily service rows.)\n2) The payer-specific SNF guideline for Aetna Medicare Advantage was not available in the dataset; the reviewer fell back to a payer-agnostic reference that also requires confirmation of a qualifying prior inpatient hospital stay to establish skilled coverage. No documentation of a qualifying hospital stay was returned in the retrieved rows, so the required coverage precondition cannot be confirmed from the record provided.\n\nBecause the audit must examine every billed date and confirm plan-specific admission criteria, and because the retrievals do not include therapy-session documentation for 2026-05-28 through 2026-06-08 nor a qualifying hospital stay, there is insufficient evidence in the material provided to determine whether the billed 0191 per-diem level is supported for the entire 2026-05-12 to 2026-06-08 range. If the provider supplies the missing items (therapy notes/minutes for 2026-05-28 through 2026-06-08, the qualifying hospital discharge/admission documentation, and the payer-specific per-diem guideline if available), the auditor can complete a definitive day-by-day determination.\n\nCited items used in this determination are listed below (verbatim excerpts):\n- Therapy session entries showing daily minutes (examples): {\"service_date\": \"2026-05-12\", \"note_title\": \"Physical Therapy\", \"revenue_code\": \"0421\", \"minutes\": 90, \"billable_units\": 6} ; {\"service_date\": \"2026-05-12\", \"note_title\": \"Occupational Therapy\", \"revenue_code\": \"0431\", \"minutes\": 60, \"billable_units\": 4}.\n- Per-diem-level extraction result for the claim showing null level determinations on each date (example row): {\"service_date\": \"2026-05-12\", \"level_determination_statement\": null} and the retrieval note: \"level_determination_statement is null on a date when the daily note doesn't state an explicit per-diem-level exception for it - that does NOT by itself mean the day is unsupported; it commonly means the billed level's own minute threshold was met that day, so the facility had no exception to document. A non-null statement is the facility's own basis for downcoding that specific date.\"\n- Reference guide policy text (fallback used because payer-specific guideline was not available): \"A prior inpatient hospital stay of the length required by the plan, immediately preceding SNF admission, that establishes the skilled need.\"; \"A service that requires the involvement of licensed nursing or therapy staff, and could not be safely or effectively provided by non-skilled caregivers.\"; and \"Standard billing codes for the four SNF per-diem levels of care referenced in these guidelines: 0191 (skilled nursing), 0192 (rehabilitation therapy), 0193 (sub-acute), 0194 (weanable ventilator management).\"\n\nNext recommended provider submissions to allow a final, date-by-date determination: (1) therapy documentation (session notes and minutes) for 2026-05-28 through 2026-06-08, (2) the hospital discharge/transfer documentation showing the prior inpatient stay that established the skilled need, (3) the facility's MDS and care plan covering the billed period, and (4) the payer-specific per-diem guideline (Aetna Medicare Advantage) if available.",
